</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" colspan="5">Before anesthesia induction (T0)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;PaO<sub>2</sub> (mmHg)</td><td align="left">98.73 &#x000b1;&#x02009;1.19</td><td align="left">98.96 &#x000b1;&#x02009;1.19</td><td align="left">98.85 &#x000b1;&#x02009;1.17</td><td align="left">0.775</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;PaCO<sub>2</sub> (mmHg)</td><td align="left">39.61 &#x000b1;&#x02009;1.83</td><td align="left">39.52 &#x000b1;&#x02009;1.92</td><td align="left">39.04 &#x000b1;&#x02009;1.56</td><td align="left">0.449</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;PH</td><td align="left">7.39 &#x000b1;&#x02009;0.018</td><td align="left">7.39 &#x000b1;&#x02009;0.017</td><td align="left">7.39 &#x000b1;&#x02009;0.015</td><td align="left">0.610</td></tr><tr><td align="left" colspan="5">At the end of the surgery (T1)</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;PaO<sub>2</sub> (mmHg)</td><td align="left">268.23 &#x000b1;&#x02009;92.75<sup>a</sup></td><td align="left">346.81 &#x000b1;&#x02009;89.87<sup>ac</sup></td><td align="left">373.48 &#x000b1;&#x02009;96.67<sup>ac</sup></td><td align="left">&#x0003c;0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;PaCO<sub>2</sub> (mmHg)</td><td align="left">48.69 &#x000b1;&#x02009;5.13<sup>ab</sup></td><td align="left">40.93 &#x000b1;&#x02009;3.68</td><td align="left">51.07 &#x000b1;&#x02009;6.86 <sup>ab</sup></td><td align="left">&#x0003c;0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;PH</td><td align="left">7.31 &#x000b1;&#x02009;0.053<sup>ab</sup></td><td align="left">7.39 &#x000b1;&#x02009;0.035</td><td align="left">7.28 &#x000b1;&#x02009;0.047 <sup>abc</sup></td><td align="left">&#x0003c;0.001</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p>Values are presented as the mean &#x000b1;&#x02009;standard deviation, Group differences were compared using one-way ANOVA, and pairwise comparisons were conducted using Bonferroni correction</p><p><sup>a</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0003c; 0.05 compared to T<sub>0</sub></p><p><sup>b</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0003c; 0.050 (considering Bonferroni correction) compared to T grop</p><p><sup>c</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0003c; 0.050 (considering Bonferroni correction) compared to M grop</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap>
</p><p id="Par34">Compared with those in Group T, the awakening time, PAED score, incidence of postoperative agitation, and incidence of postoperative nausea and vomiting in Group M and Group H were significantly lower (<italic>P</italic>&#x02009;&#x0003c; 0.05), and there were no cases of reflux aspiration (Table&#x000a0;<xref rid="Tab4" ref-type="table">4</xref>).</p><p id="Par35">
